  "goodToKnow": "Der Strafvollzug is the penal system, the carrying out of prison sentences. In Germany its main aim is Resozialisierung, preparing prisoners for a life without crime, so there's der offene Vollzug (open prison) and prisoners work and train. Prisons are officially Justizvollzugsanstalten (JVA), colloquially Knast. Since 2006, each state makes its own prison laws. It has no plural."
